=== RC-1: per-LAYER-OPCODE, LANE cycles vs RECORD-WINDOW cycles ===
  The `lop` column names the layer opcode in flight during a record's
  window.  Two different quantities can be summed against it and they
  are NOT interchangeable:
    L_CMP  = the compute LANE's own busy cycles inside the window
             (class 0).  Summed over every lop this is the whole lane,
             which is what S4 §5.3.2's per-opcode table and this
             census's 41.610 ms both are, so it is the comparable one.
    ncyc   = the record window itself, dispatch to the next record.
             It includes the sequencer's poll/fetch either side, so it
             is LARGER and is not a lane figure.
